%S A399618 1,1,5,133,14945,6997261,13675800905,111362321313013,
%T A399618 3758858977820472545,522488988772685615821021,
%U A399618 297050987727461172945066896345
%N A399618 Number of ordered n-tuples of nonempty subsets of an n-element set (repetitions allowed) such that the subsets are pairwise intersecting and cover the whole set.
%C A399618 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of n X n binary matrices with no zero column such that every two distinct rows have a common 1.
%H A399618 Vladeta Jovovic and G. Kilibarda, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1515/dma.1999.9.6.593">On the number of Boolean functions in the Post classes F_8^mu</a>, Discrete Mathematics and Applications, Vol. 9, No. 6 (1999), pp. 593-605.
%F A399618 For n >= 1, a(n) = Sum_{G subset K_n} (-1)^e(G) * (i(G) - 1)^n, where the sum is over all labeled simple graphs G on n vertices, e(G) is the number of edges of G, and i(G) is the number of independent sets of G, including the empty set.
%e A399618 a(2) = 5, corresponding to the ordered pairs ({1},{1,2}), ({2},{1,2}), ({1,2},{1}), ({1,2},{2}), and ({1,2},{1,2}).
%Y A399618 Cf. A399617, A053156, A053157, A052390.
